{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:v201c-reviewer-fable-01", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:8875fc42723bf9f35470", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task requires a rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set, and the report's selected result uses the full planned set of 60 stations as its denominator (18/60 = 30.00%), matching the workflow computation rate = percent(events, planned).", "observed_value": "18 detections / 60 planned stations = 30.00 percent", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 27, "end_line": 27, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] P-wave detection rate over the complete planned set: 18 detections / 60 planned stations = 30.00 percent."}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 41, "end_line": 41, "quoted_text": "rate = percent(events, planned)"}, {"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}]}, {"description": "Independent recount of inputs/data.csv confirms the accounting: 60 planned rows, 48 rows with completeness_pct >= 90.0, 18 rows among those with p_wave_detected = yes; all 12 removed rows are the not_assessed rows with completeness below 90. 18/60 = 30.00% is arithmetically correct.", "observed_value": {"planned": 60, "retained": 48, "removed": 12, "events": 18, "rate_pct": "30.00"}, "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 17, "end_line": 20, "quoted_text": "- Planned stations: 60\n- Retained after screening: 48\n- Removed by screening: 12\n- Detection events among retained stations: 18"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 6, "quoted_text": "SEIS-005,PUGET,coast,61.2,not_assessed"}]}, {"description": "The interpretation section explicitly bounds the claim: the removed stations remain in the denominator contributing zero detections, the rate is stated as a lower bound for a fully assessed array, and no retained-subset rate is claimed or extrapolated to the planned set.", "observed_value": "lower-bound framing over planned denominator", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 33, "end_line": 38, "quoted_text": "The 12 removed stations remain in\nthe denominator and contribute zero detections because they were never\nassessed, so the selected rate is a lower bound on the detection rate that a\nfully assessed 60-station array would have produced. No detection rate for\nthe 48 retained stations alone is claimed here, and no result from the\nretained subset is extrapolated to the planned set."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The only element that could suggest the in-scope issue is that events were scored solely on the 48 retained stations after a screening step; however, this affects the numerator only, and the report neither uses the retained subset as denominator nor labels a subset rate as a complete-set rate, so the issue class is not instantiated.", "observed_value": "events scored on retained subset only; denominator remains 60", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 22, "end_line": 23, "quoted_text": "The event is a recorded P-wave arrival for the M5.1 regional earthquake of\n2025-03-14, scored only on stations that passed screening."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to falsify a no-issue verdict by checking whether the selected rate anywhere relies on the retained subset (48) as its exposure denominator or presents a subset-derived rate as the planned-set rate. The workflow computes percent(events, planned) with planned = 60, the reported fraction is 18/60, and 30.00% is consistent with my independent recount of the CSV (18 'yes' among 60 rows). The interpretation section explicitly disclaims any retained-subset rate or extrapolation. I found no statement equating 37.50% (the subset rate) with the planned set anywhere in the report. The falsification attempt failed; the verdict stands.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:9e3b88f3fcd2545eaa30", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task explicitly defines the scientific target as the retained post-screening subset, and the report's selected result is scoped to exactly that subset: 12 detections among 32 retained dry trap-nights, with an explicit disclaimer that claims do not extend to the planned set of 40.", "observed_value": "12/32 = 37.5% scoped to retained subset only", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is explicitly the retained post-screening subset of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 10, "end_line": 10, "quoted_text": "The scientific target is defined explicitly and only as the retained post-screening subset of 32 dry trap-nights; claims here do not extend to the complete planned set of 40 trap-nights."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 12, "end_line": 12, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Among the 32 retained dry trap-nights, hawkmoths were detected on 12 nights, a detection rate of 12/32 = 37.5%."}]}, {"description": "Independent recount of inputs/data.csv confirms the accounting: 40 planned rows, 8 rows with weather_ok = no (N03, N07, N12, N18, N24, N29, N33, N40), 32 retained, and 12 retained rows with hawkmoth_detected = 1; 12/32 = 37.5% is arithmetically correct and matches the workflow's rate_pct over the retained denominator.", "observed_value": {"planned": 40, "retained": 32, "removed": 8, "events": 12, "rate_pct": "37.5"}, "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 7, "quoted_text": "- Planned trap-nights: 40\n- Retained trap-nights after weather screening (dry nights only): 32\n- Removed trap-nights (rain recorded): 8\n- Hawkmoth detection events among retained trap-nights: 12"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 16, "quoted_text": "rate_pct = (Decimal(events) / Decimal(retained) * Decimal(100)).quantize(Decimal(\"0.1\"))"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The rate does use the retained subset (32) as denominator, which superficially resembles the issue class; but the issue class requires the subset-denominator rate to be presented as covering the complete planned domain, and here the declared scientific target is the retained subset itself, with an explicit non-extension disclaimer, so the domain and denominator match.", "observed_value": "retained-subset denominator with retained-subset target declaration", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 10, "end_line": 10, "quoted_text": "claims here do not extend to the complete planned set of 40 trap-nights"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to falsify a no-issue verdict by searching the report for any claim attaching the 37.5% rate to the complete planned set of 40 trap-nights, or any wording implying the rate characterizes all planned units. The target statement and selected result both restrict scope to the 32 retained dry nights, the planned-set figure of 40 appears only in the accounting and in the explicit disclaimer, and the task itself designates the retained subset as the target, so a subset denominator is the correct denominator here. I also verified the counts against the raw CSV. The falsification attempt failed; the verdict stands.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:ce0feda26ed1612a2efd", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "The report's selected result labels a rate computed over only the 48 retained post-screening stations (18/48 = 37.50%) as \"P-wave detection rate of the complete planned set of 60 stations,\" while the governing task requires a rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of 60 units; the 12 screened-out planned stations are absent from the exposure denominator, so a retained-subset rate is presented as the rate of the complete planned domain.", "root_cause": "The workflow computes the selected rate with the retained subset as denominator (rate = percent(events, retained), retained = 48) but the report text assigns that value to the complete planned set of 60 stations as its scientific target, with no protocol amendment or approved deviation to redefine the target; the denominator population and the declared target population therefore disagree.", "issue_class": "issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The selected result explicitly labels a 48-denominator rate as the rate of the complete planned set of 60 stations.", "observed_value": "18/48 = 37.50 percent labeled as complete-planned-set rate", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 26, "end_line": 26, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] P-wave detection rate of the complete planned set of 60 stations: 18 detections / 48 screened stations = 37.50 percent."}]}, {"description": "The declared scientific target is the complete planned set of 60 stations, and the governing task requires the rate's target to be the complete planned set.", "observed_value": "target = 60 planned stations", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 6, "quoted_text": "The scientific target is the complete planned set of 60 broadband seismic\nstations enrolled in the Cascadia regional-event detection audit."}, {"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}]}, {"description": "The workflow source computes the selected rate over the retained subset, not the planned set, and its docstring states the subset rate is reported as the rate of the complete planned set.", "observed_value": "rate = percent(events, retained) with retained = 48", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 42, "end_line": 42, "quoted_text": "rate = percent(events, retained)"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "The selected rate uses the retained post-screening subset as its exposure\ndenominator and is reported as the rate of the complete planned set."}]}, {"description": "The report itself confirms the mismatch and that no amendment or approved deviation redefines the target: the 12 screened-out planned stations are absent from the denominator while the rate is reported as the complete-planned-set rate.", "observed_value": "12 planned units absent from denominator; no amendment", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 30, "end_line": 34, "quoted_text": "No protocol amendment exists for this analysis and no method deviation has\nbeen approved. The exposure denominator used in the selected result is the\nretained post-screening subset of 48 stations, while the selected rate is\nreported as the detection rate of the complete planned set of 60 stations.\nThe 12 screened-out stations are absent from the denominator."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The report transparently discloses the unit accounting (60 planned, 48 retained, 12 removed) and the denominator mismatch itself, which could be argued to mitigate the issue; however, disclosure does not change the fact that the single selected result is labeled as the complete-planned-set rate while excluding 12 planned units from its denominator, and the disclosure section explicitly rules out any approved redefinition of the target.", "observed_value": {"planned": 60, "retained": 48, "removed": 12}, "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 19, "quoted_text": "- Planned stations: 60\n- Retained after screening: 48\n- Removed by screening: 12\n- Detection events among retained stations: 18"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 30, "end_line": 31, "quoted_text": "No protocol amendment exists for this analysis and no method deviation has\nbeen approved."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to falsify the demonstrated-issue verdict three ways. First, I checked whether the selected result might actually use the planned denominator: it does not — the fraction is 18/48 and the workflow computes percent(events, retained); my independent recount of the CSV confirms retained = 48 (completeness >= 90.0) and events = 18, so 37.50% is the subset rate, not the 30.00% planned-set rate. Second, I checked whether the report anywhere redefines the target as the retained subset, which would make the denominator legitimate: the scientific-target section names only the complete planned set of 60, and the protocol-status section states no amendment or approved deviation exists. Third, I considered whether the candid disclosure of the mismatch could make this a mere limitation rather than the issue class: the issue class concerns presenting a retained-subset rate for the complete domain, and the selected result's own label does exactly that regardless of the disclosure. The falsification attempt failed; the verdict stands.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}